## Report

### 1. Built
- **`crates/umber-app/src/paint_state.rs`** (only app file touched):
  - `begin_stroke_styled` paint arm now opens a `PaintStrokeCapture` instead of `retouch_history.clear()` (v1 clear gone); mask/retouch arms explicitly set it to `None`.
  - New `PaintTileCapture`/`PaintStrokeCapture` structs (module scope): lazy per-tile before snapshot + dirty-rect union.
  - New `capture_paint_event` hook in `push_event_styled`, running on the FINAL staged dabs (post symmetry expansion + mask gate) so siblings are covered; seam mirrors recurse through the same staging. First staged batch per tile drains + reads back (earlier strokes in the bytes); readback failure records nothing without dropping the stamp.
  - `end_stroke` finalizes via new `finish_paint_capture`: drain + read back each touched tile, slice AFTER bytes from the same rect, skip identity/resize-mismatched/unreadable tiles, push ONE `PaintStrokeCommand` (reused type, no new command) on the shared history, drop the queued re-apply like the retouch path.
  - Module docs: full paint-undo section + per-entry cost math (512² worst-case entry ~2 MiB → entry cap binds; 4K worst-case entry ~128 MiB → byte budget binds; typical r=24 stroke tens of KiB) and the v1 verdict (keep both caps, no `on_evict`).
  - 2 new GPU-gated tests: `paint_stroke_undoes_and_redoes_byte_exact`, `two_paint_strokes_undo_reverts_only_the_latest`. All existing mask/symmetry/retouch/seam/routing tests untouched.
- **`crates/umber-brush/src/retouch.rs`**: `footprint` promoted `pub(crate)` → `pub` with a sharing rationale doc (the shader-identical box is now the paint capture's dirty-rect source; single definition so it can't drift).

### 2. Judgment calls (all also in module docs)
- Reused `PaintStrokeCommand`/`TileRegion` as-is; undo/redo flow through `retouch_writes` unchanged.
- Last-stroke undo is byte-exact; older-under-newer overlap is linear-undo last-write-wins (retouch already had this property) — no rect merging.
- 2 readbacks per touched tile per paint stroke (before + after) are inherent — paint has no CPU mirror to hold the after in.
- before==after tiles and empty strokes record no entry (identity rule, mirrors retouch).
- Mask strokes still bypass history; `resize_target` still clears it.
- Kept both caps (64 entries + 256 MiB), no `on_evict` (evicted `Vec<u8>` needs no cleanup); entry cap must never rise toward 100 without the byte budget.

### 3. Unverified
- GPU behavior (undo byte-exactness, redo, two-stroke isolation) needs a wgpu adapter — the new tests follow the existing `try_request_device` skip pattern and were typechecked via clippy `--all-targets` but **not executed** here (`cargo test` is forbidden; CI is the runtime gate).
